@@ -20,3 +20,10 @@
 - Corridors have post-construction wall torches every six distinct pathway cells (rather than unreliable provisional torches on exterior cave stone). Every room gets four supported wall torches. Existing recessed shaft Glowstone remains unchanged.
 - Zombies (including subclasses) and all vanilla skeleton variants target Gnomes through the normal AI target-goal selector, while retaining normal player priority. Neutral Gnomes still retaliate and alert village allies when attacked.
 - New generation only. Existing generated villages remain unchanged.
+
+## v0.3.90 — sealed village, widened stair bends, rectangular rooms, Glowshrooms
+
+- Every intentional air pocket receives a solid-block shell where it borders natural cave air or fluid. Only the 2×2 portal at the end of the cavern entrance corridor is excluded. The existing pair of oak entrance doors remains.
+- Spiral stair construction uses one cardinally adjacent outer lane at every step, plus corner infill. Radial rounding no longer collapses the second lane.
+- All rooms remain axis-aligned rectangles. Galleries end at their entrance wall, not in the middle of the furnished room.
+- Newly placed luminous mushrooms are `syntacticwizardry:glowshroom` (light level 14), with renamed textures, models, item, loot table and translation. The previous Growshroom registry remains hidden and loadable for worlds saved with v0.3.89.
